### Slice B: artefacts and captures. VS Code extension "REST Client" (humao.rest-client).
### Send the requests top to bottom. Nothing secret is stored in this file.
### Local server: http://localhost:8000. Deployed: put the Render URL below.

@baseUrl = https://YOUR-HOST

### 0. Sign in (owned by A; included so the later requests have a token).
### Login takes "username". If this returns 400, try "email" instead.
# @name login
# @prompt username Your username
# @prompt password Your password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token/
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{username}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.access}}

### 1. Create an artefact (researcher). 201 and the new record, starting as Draft.
### nmk_accession_no must be unique: use a new value on every run.
# @name createArtefact
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/artefacts/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nmk_accession_no": "DEMO-E2E-001",
  "title": "DEMO: e2e test object",
  "community": "Demo community",
  "object_type": "Vessel",
  "materials": "Clay (demo)",
  "height_mm": "240.0",
  "width_mm": "180.0",
  "depth_mm": "180.0"
}

###
@artefactId = {{createArtefact.response.body.$.id}}

### 2. Fetch one artefact. 404 if it does not exist or is not visible to you.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/artefacts/{{artefactId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Start a capture. 201 with id, expires_in and four signed upload links.
# @name startCapture
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/artefacts/{{artefactId}}/captures/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Upload the four photos straight to storage with the signed links.
### Do NOT add an Authorization header: the link carries its own signature and storage
### rejects a request that has two. Content-Type must be exactly image/jpeg. Success is 200.
### Put four harmless JPEGs (never NMK photos) in ./sample-photos/ as front, back, left, right.
PUT {{startCapture.response.body.$.upload_urls.front}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample-photos/front.jpg

###
PUT {{startCapture.response.body.$.upload_urls.back}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample-photos/back.jpg

###
PUT {{startCapture.response.body.$.upload_urls.left}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample-photos/left.jpg

###
PUT {{startCapture.response.body.$.upload_urls.right}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample-photos/right.jpg

### 5. Complete the capture. Checks all four photos exist, then returns upload_complete true and views.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/artefacts/captures/{{startCapture.response.body.$.id}}/complete/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Search (step 8 of the e2e script). Returns { count, next, previous, results }.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/artefacts/?q=e2e&limit=20&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6b. Filters: community and object_type (case-insensitive exact), status (draft, in_collection, withdrawn).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/artefacts/?community=Demo%20community&status=draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
